Add theme tokens: data-driven visual control of the whole site

The site's colours, glow, motion and canvas depth are now stored as a row in
theme_settings rather than living only in CSS, so the admin assistant can propose
a visual change and have it apply with no build and no deploy.

- Ten tokens with hard clamps: three accent hues, saturation, glow, motion speed,
  canvas depth, hue cycling, contrast and grain. Plus five named vibe presets.
- get_theme (read) and propose_theme_change (write) tools. A theme change goes
  through the same proposal, fingerprint and undo path as every other change.
- lib/theme.ts is the single source of truth for the token vocabulary.
  scripts/sync-theme-tokens.mjs copies it into the Edge Function directory, since
  a function cannot import from ../../lib. Run it after editing lib/theme.ts.
- ThemeProvider applies the tokens as CSS custom properties on the document, so
  one change moves the storefront and the admin panel together.
- index.css styles are additive and opt-in behind [data-tb-theme="on"], so if the
  theme fails to load the site keeps exactly its previous appearance.
- Confirmation cards render hue swatches, since a bare number tells you nothing
  about the colour you are about to approve.
